<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The app makes three classes of network request, and no others. Basemap vector tiles from
  tiles.openfreemap.org, issued by MapLibre. Reachability probes bound to the cellular network,
  which connect and hand-shake and send nothing. And, from the uplink-asymmetry probe, an 8 KB
  POST to speed.cloudflare.com.

  That POST is the only upload this app performs, and it is worth being exact about what it
  contains, because an earlier version of this comment said there was no upload path at all: the
  body is 8,192 bytes from a fixed-seed PRNG, byte-for-byte identical on every cycle, pseudo-random
  only so that a compressing proxy cannot shrink it and flatter the measurement. It carries no
  collected data, no device identifier and nothing about the user. **No measurement this app
  records has an upload path**, which remains true and is the claim that matters.

  There is no analytics and no crash reporter.

  targetSdk 36 already defaults cleartext to off; this states it rather than inheriting it, so a
  future dependency cannot quietly re-enable plaintext HTTP for its own fetches. User-added CA
  certificates are not trusted either — none of this traffic carries anything the user would want
  to inspect, and nothing in this app needs to be interceptable by a proxy they did not install
  for it.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
</network-security-config>
